        "_id": "6161a61a2c0de966b4e43486",
        "alias": "Razzmatazz Eagle",
        "aliasID": "65c2b7efed6eefce4c4dceae",
        "anonymized": false,
        "avatarURL": "https://canny.io/images/f9b909781ec10a9c42837d9eafdd9561.png",
        "created": "2021-10-09T14:24:26.758Z",
        "name": "Kung",
        "serviceAccount": false,
        "urlName": null
      },
      "authorID": null,
      "boardID": "5b0746088fa72313783e3269",
      "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
      "created": "2024-03-25T19:02:40.271Z",
      "deleted": false,
      "fileURLs": [],
      "files": [],
      "imageURLs": [],
      "integrationSourceType": null,
      "internal": false,
      "itemSourceType": null,
      "mentionedUserIDs": null,
      "mentionedUsers": [],
      "mergeID": null,
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "65fcf9f615ad1e7de2bb30a9",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This is marked (automatically) as \"Available in a future release\" because internally the issue is resolved as being handled by an update to our docs to explain that the expected head drift that can happen with lock hips may not always play well with the VRCHeadChop component.\n\nAs others have mentioned it would create positional desync to force the VRCHeadChop to lock in while the avatar's head is unlocked and allowed to slide, with knock-on effects for network (including remote users grabbing physbones on your hair) as well as a local desync between your avatar in the mirror and first person. In general, there a various small issues that can appear on avatars as a result of the sliding that's possible when the IK mode setting allows that part to slide. Rather than trying to make all edge cases work in all modes, the whole reason the options exist is to allow users to pick the mode with the least issues and run with that. In this case the intended design is to use lock head or lock both to solve the issue.\n\nAlso, thanks for the suggestions and advice about the default IK mode as well as your other points. Personally I agree with having Lock Head be the default, but during the IK Beta(s) trying to change any default behavior led to wide spread confusion so there have been minimal changes there (the old IK allowed the head to drift with no alternative to lock anything in). The addition of this component is an extra nudge though to reconsider the default lock mode. It might be less confusing if the default is changed in an update that doesn't have other IK changes.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
